## 2. Before writing any code

Stop with `{{blocked_status}}` if any item is missing:

- [ ] Approved: {{gates}} <!-- GEN: user approvals only -->
- [ ] {{prep_phase_rule}} <!-- GEN: e.g. "PHASE-00 ticked [x] PREPARED / COMPLETED"; delete if no preparation phase -->
- [ ] Every phase in `{{dependency_notation}}` has passed
- [ ] The current branch is the one the plan or decision record names ({{branch_rule}})
- [ ] Each task names its files, reused components/contracts, a check command and its expected result
- [ ] {{validator_rule}} <!-- GEN: e.g. a dossier validator command; delete if none -->

A missing item is a **planning gap**: report it to {{planner_role}} through {{plan_change_process}} and stop. Do not fill it in yourself.

## 3. Sources of truth

- Requirements and acceptance criteria: `{{requirements_source}}`
- Contracts (API, data): `{{contract_source}}`
- Never re-query external systems for data the plan already recorded, and never invent business records, services or fallbacks.

## 4. Pre-flight before task 1

1. Read `{{global_constraints_section}}` and `{{review_focus_section}}`: constraints bind every task; review focus names inputs the reviewer will try, so plan tests or guards for them now.
2. Build the Consumes / Produces table: one row per edge between tasks, or between a task and existing code. Open the existing symbol and compare the **real** signature.

| Consumer task | Consumes (as the plan states it) | Producer (task or existing `path:symbol`) | Produces (real signature) | Finding |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| {{task}} | {{consumes}} | {{producer}} | {{produces}} | OK / Mismatch → {{plan_change_id}} |

3. Any mismatch, missing producer, task contradicting a global constraint, or check that cannot work → raise a plan change before coding and return `{{blocked_status}}`.

A phase whose tasks share nothing gets the single line `Pre-flight: no shared interfaces`. A clean table is still written down.

